Real-agent verification evidence: I ran `cargo run --bin work-leaf -- --agent codex` inside a 100x30 PTY through Work Leaf, using the configured Codex backend. In the terminal UI I submitted `:new Reply exactly with WORK_LEAF_VISUAL_AGENT_OK and do not modify files.`, and the real agent chat became visible with `codex: Codex session 019ef4a2-f776-7e01-867a-4d6bdcaf4a2d` plus `WORK_LEAF_VISUAL_AGENT_OK`.

Then I sent `Esc` followed by `v`. The final visible Work Leaf frame showed `mode=visual-char focus=right window=1/1`, and the chat pane still showed the real agent reply with the first selected cell reversed as `\x1b[7mW\x1b[0mORK_LEAF_VISUAL_AGENT_OK`. The script exited 2 only because its literal substring check did not strip that ANSI reverse-video marker; the captured frame demonstrates the requested real terminal/agent-chat visual selection behavior.

